Plumix — Third-Party Provenance & Attribution
=============================================

This is a curated record of source-level code that Plumix has copied or
adapted from upstream projects, and where it deliberately diverges from a
dependency. It is NOT a generated software bill of materials (SBOM): it does
not enumerate the licenses of Plumix's npm dependencies, whose notices travel
with the installed packages. It covers only code that lives in Plumix's own
source tree by way of copying, porting, or adaptation.

Every license below was verified from the upstream's own LICENSE at the source
cited, not from memory. Plumix itself is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE).

Entries are grouped by derivation depth:

  1. Copied / adapted code — an upstream MIT notice is reproduced, as required.
  2. Dependency divergence — Plumix's own code that replaces a dependency's
     behavior; no upstream code is copied, so no notice is owed.
  3. Prior art / inspiration — idea-level influence only; no code was copied
     and no notice is owed. Listed for honesty, never as code derivation.


1. Copied / adapted code
------------------------

shadcn/ui — MIT — Copyright (c) 2023 shadcn
  Verified: https://github.com/shadcn-ui/ui/blob/main/LICENSE.md
  Derived surface: packages/admin-ui/src/ — the vendored shadcn/ui primitive
    components, kept byte-identical to upstream so `shadcn diff` upgrades apply
    cleanly. See packages/admin-ui/src/NOTICE for the per-file detail and the
    exceptions (components that are original Plumix work, not shadcn/ui).

Astro — MIT — Copyright (c) 2021 Fred K. Schott
  Verified: https://github.com/withastro/astro/blob/main/LICENSE
  Derived surface:
    - packages/blocks/src/island-element.ts   (port of `astro-island.ts`)
    - packages/blocks/src/serialize.ts        (port of Astro's prop serializer;
                                               PROP_TYPE codes + wire format)
    - packages/blocks/src/static-html.tsx     (adaptation of Astro's `StaticHtml`)
    - packages/blocks/src/island-strategies/  (hydration triggers, adapted)
  Kept: the SSR/client island wire format and prop-serialization scheme, which
    are a hard contract between server and client.
  Diverged: chunk-retry on failed import, a cancelable hydration-error event,
    event-replay on the interaction strategy, and strategy timeout handling.

Nuxt — MIT — Copyright (c) 2016-present Nuxt Team
  Verified: https://github.com/nuxt/nuxt/blob/main/LICENSE
  Derived surface: packages/blocks/src/island-strategies/ — the `visible` and
