2. Dependency divergence
------------------------

@oslojs/crypto — MIT
  Plumix reimplements SEC1-uncompressed public-key encoding in
  packages/core/src/auth/passkey/register.ts (`encodeSec1Uncompressed`) rather
  than using the dependency's `ECDSAPublicKey.encodeSEC1Uncompressed`, which
  left-aligns the Y coordinate and silently corrupts ~1/256 of P-256 keys (a
  leading-zero Y). This bug is still present in the latest release (1.0.1). The
  reimplementation copies no upstream code — it produces the standard RFC 5480
  §2.2 format that the dependency's own decoder reads back correctly. Remove it
  once a fixed, usably-exposed upstream release ships.


3. Prior art / inspiration (no code copied; not a derivation)
-------------------------------------------------------------

These influenced Plumix's design or behavior but contributed no copied code.
No attribution is owed; they are listed for transparency.

  - drizzle-query-logger (MIT, https://github.com/max-programming/drizzle-query-logger)
      — the idea of syntax-highlighting SQL in logs; Plumix's
        packages/core/src/debug-bar/highlight-sql.ts is an independent
        implementation targeting CSS token spans.
  - WordPress (GPL) — behavioral parity for hierarchical taxonomies, bulk
      actions, and user-management UX. GPL code is NOT copied into Plumix, and
      this parity must never be recorded as code derivation.
  - Puck, Builder.io, Solid — concept-level references for the editor and
      reactivity design.


